From 8284d0b520c3b7e83c15de883b14fb4f50fb260a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 22:53:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02449/11362] [outer-loop] bridge v2 live port: A*
 value-routing helps best-first, NOT the live depth-first explorer

Ported the v2 value head's A*-routing (depth + weight*value) into the live StepwiseExplorer +
pointed the loader at the richer v2 head. Measured live vs the 8/32 baseline.

RESULT: A* weight 5 in the LIVE explorer = 6/32 (REGRESS: lost cd82,m0r0) AND the cn04 unlock did
NOT transfer. Root cause: the offline win came from graph_explore_solve_v2, which is BEST-FIRST
(A* over the value heuristic) -- that's where richer value routing helps (it unlocked cn04, a
reachable floor win, where BFS and the v1 5-feature head both failed). The live StepwiseExplorer
is depth-first-ride + frontier-jump, a structurally different search; A* frontier weighting just
misroutes its shallow wins and does not pick up the best-first benefit.

Complete bridge scoreboard (frame-only, vs the offline oracle's 32 levels):
  baseline live explorer (BFS)                          8/32
  v1 head (5 feat) frontier-override                    3/32  regress
  v1 head depth-primary tiebreak                        8/32  neutral
  v2 head (41 feat) -- graph_explore A* (offline)       UNLOCKS cn04 (1/6 floor; v1 cannot)
  v2 head -- live StepwiseExplorer A* w5                6/32  regress, cn04 does NOT transfer
  E3 world-model induction (gemma-4-12B)                0/6 gap-1 games
Diagnostic: the floor wins are REACHABLE (oracle actions 91-100% in the candidate set) -- the
limit is ROUTING, not action-generation. So a value head CAN help -- but only a BEST-FIRST search.

SAFE STATE: the submitted agent (make_carnot_agent -> E3AgentPolicy) is pure BFS (value_weight=0
default); A* value-routing is opt-in via the eval's --value-weight. No default-agent regression.

THE TWO NEXT LEVERS (this is the honest payoff of measuring live):
  1. BEST-FIRST live explorer -- refactor StepwiseExplorer to the best-first form so the routing
     that unlocked cn04 transfers to the SUBMITTED agent. The way to cash the value-head bridge.
  2. STRONGER world-model induction -- bigger proposer / RFT it on our banked solves (deep games).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
